<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarapacá</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarapacá is a desert region in the far north of Chile, with its capital at Iquique. Formerly a Peruvian province rich in nitrates, it was conquered by Chile in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-pacific">War of the Pacific</a> and ceded under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ancon">Treaty of Ancón</a> of 1883. Its nitrate fields became the mainstay of Chilean exports and public revenue until the rise of synthetic nitrates after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarapaca.jpg" alt="Tarapacá" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Criss Salazar · CC BY 2.0 cl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iglesia_de_Tarapac%C3%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
